dialogue 5 3 "older_woman" "First time this far west?"
dialogue 9 3 "hero" "First time past the river."
dialogue 13 5 "older_man" "What takes you out there? Work, or someone waiting?"
dialogue 19 6 "hero" "My family. They've done well out west. They sent for me."
dialogue 26 5 "older_woman" "Then at least you'll have a roof when you get there."
dialogue 32 5 "older_man" "And someone to tell you how much the place has changed."
dialogue 38 4 "hero" "I think they'll have more to say about how little I have."
dialogue 42 3 "older_woman" "Oh, families always do."
dialogue 46 4 "older_man" "That ridge was there a moment ago."
dialogue 51 4 "older_woman" "Can the driver still see the track?"
dialogue 63 5 "conductor" "Easy now, folks. Nobody's hurt. Stay in your seats."
dialogue 69 8 "conductor" "Don't be afraid. There's an army fort just around the bend. We'll shelter there until this blows over."
